# Cloudflare Pages response headers.
#
# This rule works for the portal's HTML pages: they come back
# `no-cache, must-revalidate`, so a browser always re-checks them and picks
# up a new deploy immediately.
#
# It does NOT work for .js/.css. Pages overrides Cache-Control on static
# assets with its own `max-age=14400` (4 hours) regardless of what is
# written here — verified against the live site after this file shipped.
# That is why every portal script and stylesheet is referenced with a
# `?v=N` version string in the HTML instead (see team/README.md). Since the
# HTML is always revalidated, bumping N is what actually forces browsers
# onto new JS. Do not remove the versioning and assume this file covers it.
/team/*
  Cache-Control: no-cache, must-revalidate
